			},
			"date": "2022-11-10T15:09:42.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> IMO a good way to think about it is that when you boost a post, it has the same effect as if you publish a post yourself. All your followers will see it, and it also will be seen in the local timeline of your server (that is only you in your case, ha).</p><p>I actually like that when you boost in Mastodon, your avatar is shown a bit smaller than the original poster but it clearly shows that you are the one giving it a boost. I think it is good for taking accountability of what we boost</p>",
